+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every registered tool declares an `inputSchema` in JSON Schema format (`src/types/ai.ts`) that is handed to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates incoming model arguments against that schema before calling the tool's executor. A malformed tool call returns a `ToolResponse` describing the failure so the model can correct its call on the next tool round instead of terminating the conversation stream with an unhandled exception.
+
+## Validation contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before calling the executor; on failure it returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` describes the failure, and the executor is never invoked ([validated by: rejects a call missing a required field with a ToolResponse and never invokes the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L27)).
+- Validation enforces `required`, declared types and `enum` only: it does not inject `additionalProperties: false`, coerce types, or apply defaults, so valid input with an unlisted extra property is passed through to the executor unchanged ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field without leaking the offending value in the response or logs, and passes valid input with extra properties unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L43)).
+- A wrong-typed field is rejected with a message naming the field path and the expected type, and neither the rejection text nor any log line produced during the call contains the offending property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field without leaking the offending value in the response or logs, and passes valid input with extra properties unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L43)).
+- Because a schema rejection resolves to a `ToolResponse` rather than throwing, `createChatOrchestrator` feeds the rejection text back to the provider as a `tool_result` message on the next round within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns the schema rejection to the model as a tool_result on the next round so the orchestrator loop recovers on retry](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L127)).
+- Calling `execute` with an unregistered tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>`.
+
+## Schema compilation
+
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled once at `register` time, and an uncompilable schema causes `register` to throw synchronously with a message naming the tool so a broken schema fails at startup rather than mid-conversation ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool for an uncompilable static schema and validates function-valued definitions against the current call schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L79)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each call and validates against the schema current at that call, caching compiled validators by the resolved schema object ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool for an uncompilable static schema and validates function-valued definitions against the current call schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L79)).
